.git
.gitignore
# **/ for the reason given above __pycache__ below: a bare pattern would
# exclude only a tarball or PDF at the context root, and AC6 means all of them.
**/*.tar
**/*.pdf
docs/
static/earnings/
static/uploads/
config/keys.json
# Unlike .gitignore, a bare dockerignore pattern matches only the build
# context root -- it needs an explicit **/ to reach the __pycache__ and *.pyc
# that exist at every depth under app/, db/ and exchange/ (verified by
# building docker/Dockerfile: without the prefix these ship into the image).
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.venv/
config/.jwt_secret

# Added for v2 (plan T10) — this repository's own junk, absent from v1.
# **/ so a web/.env.local cannot ride `COPY web/` into the build stage and have
# its VITE_* values baked into the shipped bundle.
**/.env*
# Same **/ requirement as __pycache__ above -- web/node_modules is nested, a
# bare `node_modules` entry excludes nothing and the build-context copy would
# otherwise clobber the install this Dockerfile's web-build stage just ran.
**/node_modules
legacy/
tests/
.github/
web/dist
